# Netlify proxy rules — processed in order, first match wins.
# The ! suffix = force (apply even if a function exists at the path).
#
# Intentionally empty of /api/* and /uploads/* rules.
#
# A rule here cannot read environment variables, so proxying to the backend
# from this file would mean hardcoding the API host and changing it in two
# places on every environment move. Both paths are proxied in-app instead,
# reading NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL at request time:
#
#   /api/auth/*   app/api/auth/*            (needs to forward Set-Cookie itself)
#   /api/*        app/api/[...path]         (all verbs, generic pass-through)
#   /uploads/*    app/uploads/[...path]     (user media)
#
# This file previously carried `/uploads/* /uploads/:splat 200!`, which pointed
# at itself rather than at the backend and served nothing.
